      "note": "The group includes benzodiazepines, zolpidem, antipsychotics, opioids, gabapentin and pregabalin, other antiepileptics, bladder antimuscarinics, promethazine, diuretics, alpha-blockers, nitrates and centrally acting blood pressure medicines. A different antidepressant can count as the further fall-risk medicine. Generic packs that show the ingredient name with a company name count too. Count the added oral products and Transiderm-Nitro patches. Panadeine Forte contains codeine. Count the listed diuretic combinations through their indapamide or hydrochlorothiazide ingredient."
