  "rule_for_models": "Suspect a finding when the person is aged 65 or over and the record shows a supply of a Group A medicine (an antidepressant) AND a co-prescribed supply of a different medicine that raises the risk of falls, including a second antidepressant from Group A or a medicine from Group B, and the supply dates overlap or fall within 60 days of each other. One supply of each is enough. A second antidepressant must have a different active ingredient from the first. Exclude a pair when the record explicitly documents that one medicine stopped before the other began. A switch does not exclude another qualifying pair used together. If age at supply is unknown and the medicine criteria are met, report only a possible finding and ask whether the person was aged 65 or over at supply. An age below 65 rules out this finding.",
  "cannot_be_seen": "Whether the person has fallen, how well the person walks, the doses really taken, and medicines bought without a prescription or supplied by a hospital or another pharmacy.",
  "ask_the_gp": "A review of the antidepressant and of the other fall-risk medicine together, and whether either can be stopped or reduced.",
  "urgency": "routine",
  "draft": false,
  "signed_by_clinical_reviewer": { "name": "Marwan Morsy (PHA0002761764)", "date": "2026-11-20" }
